{title: It Is Well with My Soul}
{artist: Horatio Spafford}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 66}

Verse 1
When [C]peace like a [F]river at[C]tendeth my [G]way,
when [C]sorrows like [F]sea billows [G]roll —
what[C]ever my [F]lot, thou hast [C]taught me to [G]say,
"It is [C]well, it is [F]well with my [C]soul."

Chorus
It is [G]well with my [C]soul,
it is [F]well, it is [G]well with my [C]soul.

Verse 2
Though [C]Satan should buffet, [F]though [C]trials should [G]come,
Let this [F]blest assurance control,
[C]That Christ [F]has regarded [C]my helpless es [G]tate,
And hath [C]shed His own [F]blood for my [C]soul.

Verse 3
My [C]sin, oh, the bliss [F]of this [C]glorious thought! My [G]sin,
not [C]in part but [G]the whole,
[C]Is nailed [F]to the cross, and [C]I bear it no [G]more,
Praise the [C]Lord, praise the [F]Lord, O my [C]soul!

Verse 4
For [C]me, be it Christ, [F]be it [C]Christ hence to [G]live:
If [C]Jordan above me shall [F]roll, No pang [G]shall be mine,
[C]for in death as in life [G]Thou
wilt whisper Thy peace [F]to my [C]soul.

Verse 5
But, [C]Lord, 'tis for Thee, [F]for [C]Thy coming we [G]wait,
The [C]sky, not [F]the grave, is [G]our goal;
[C]Oh trump of [F]the angel! Oh voice [C]of the Lord! Blessèd [G]hope,
blessèd [C]rest of my soul!
